{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"agent_message","text":"I traced the recovery failure to the replacement graphics context returning `null` immediately after device loss. I’m adding a delayed retry while keeping input and simulation running. Touch actions now stay queued until a simulation step consumes them, which should also handle quick taps during a slow frame.\n"}}
